jsonpatch-rs ports the diff algorithm of python-json-patch 1.47
(https://github.com/stefankoegl/python-json-patch, BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2011 Stefan Kögl)
from Python to Rust. The DiffBuilder logic (runs, moves, array labels, operation order) is translated
line by line, so that the generated patches are identical.

src/seqmatch.rs is a port of CPython's difflib.SequenceMatcher (PSF-2.0), used by the diff exactly
like jsonpatch uses difflib.

tests/upstream/ contains python-json-patch's own test files (BSD-3-Clause), unchanged, used to check
that the accelerated module passes the original test suite.

orig/ holds unmodified copies of jsonpatch.py and jsonpointer.py 1.47/3.12 (BSD-3-Clause, Stefan Kögl) for reference.
